      "reason": "The probability estimate (67.82%) matches the calibrated_pd in p1. The strongest driver is correctly identified as the payment delay of 2 months in September 2005 (f1), which corresponds to the PAY_0 feature with attribution a1 (1.669 log-odds), the largest absolute contribution among all attributions (a1: 1.669, a2: 0.9678, a3: 0.2656, a4: -0.2141). Although the claim refers to 'observed payment delay' rather than the feature name 'PAY_0', this is a plain-language restatement consistent with the evidence. No rule is violated; the model's strongest driver is accurately described."
